{
 "_doc": "Scene Kit material library v0. Keys are semantic presets; a scene's material label (e.g. 'aged_brass', 'wet_stone_floor') is resolved by kit.js to the best preset via aliases/tokens, then modifiers (aged/wet/polished/dark/...) adjust it. 'tex' = Poly Haven asset id (CC0, fetched by fetch_textures.py; tile size comes from the asset's real dimensions). Presets without 'tex' are parametric PBR. Colours are linear-ish sRGB hex. Resolution: pass 1 matches preset keys + 'aliases' (material words); pass 2 matches 'objects' (object words that imply a material) only if pass 1 found nothing. Presets may carry emissive/emissiveIntensity. Presets with \"surface\": true (water) are SURFACE EFFECTS: hidden in the clay pass (no disc in the L2R layout) and given screen-space reflections in the lit pass.",
